# Unity text assets MUST be LF — Unity's YAML reader is LF-native; CRLF breaks
# parsing (e.g. empty sequence scalars), as it did to TagManager.asset.
*.asset      text eol=lf
*.unity      text eol=lf
*.prefab     text eol=lf
*.meta       text eol=lf
*.mat        text eol=lf
*.anim       text eol=lf
*.controller text eol=lf
*.physicMaterial text eol=lf
*.asmdef     text eol=lf
*.uss        text eol=lf
*.uxml       text eol=lf

# BUT binary-serialized .asset files (TerrainData / NavMesh / LightingData) are NOT YAML —
# the `*.asset text eol=lf` rule above EOL-mangles them (strips CR bytes on commit -> the
# committed blob is corrupt -> Unity "Unknown error occurred while loading" -> null TerrainData,
# the 2026-06-30 OuterWorld terrain bug). Force these binary so git stores them verbatim.
# (More-specific rules win over the *.asset rule above.)
*TerrainData.asset  binary
NavMesh-*.asset     binary
LightingData.asset  binary

# Same class of bug for the DUNGEON-CHAIN scenes: DungeonChainBuilder creates them via
# EditorSceneManager.NewScene + SaveScene in BATCHMODE, which writes them BINARY even though the
# project is ForceText (proven 2026-06-30: mode=ForceText yet firstByte=0x00; ForceReserializeAssets
# / OpenScene+SaveScene will NOT convert headlessly, only the interactive GUI editor does). Under the
# `*.unity text eol=lf` rule above a future bake could emit a CRLF in the binary data and corrupt the
# blob. These three are builder-generated + never hand-edited (CLAUDE.md §3), so force them binary so
# git stores them verbatim. (More-specific rules win over *.unity above.)
Assets/Scenes/Outpost1.unity  binary
Assets/Scenes/Dungeon.unity   binary
Assets/Scenes/Outpost2.unity  binary
# Same class again: the Room Forge composer (DungeonBaker) writes DungeonCompose scenes
# BINARY in batchmode (58% NUL, proven 2026-07-24 architect review) even under ForceText.
# Under the *.unity text eol=lf rule a renormalize/clone would EOL-mangle the blob and
# reproduce the d4_sunken_crypt corruption. Force them binary (builder-generated, never hand-edited).
Assets/Scenes/DungeonCompose/*.unity binary
# THIRD instance of the same class, and the one that was missed both previous times.
# KayKitChallengeOutpostBuilder writes this scene via EditorSceneManager.NewScene + SaveScene in
# batchmode, so it is BINARY (measured 2026-08-08: 53% NUL) exactly like the three above - but it
# was never added to this list, so `git check-attr` resolved it as `text: set, eol: lf`.
# It has survived on luck: 749 LONE CR bytes and ZERO CRLF pairs, so nothing has been eaten yet.
# One bake that emits a single 0D 0A and the next renormalize/clone silently drops a byte -
# the d4_sunken_crypt corruption, on the scene that is the whole challenge outpost.
# Flagged in docs/MASTER_CATALOG/editor-tools.md:781 ("same exposure class") and never actioned.
Assets/Scenes/KayKitChallengeOutpost.unity binary

